BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AudaTours Worcester Audio Tour: Statues\, Spires & Civic Stories U
 nveiled
DTSTART:20260207T000000
DTEND:20261231T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:491991fc587a99980c8d480a4ef305@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A bronze turtle watches as legends rise and fall in Worcester
 ’s streets\, its gaze as steady as the city’s restless spirit. Behind 
 the bustle and brick lie stories lurking in plain sight-whispers of revolu
 tion\, resilience\, and reinvention. Set off on this self-guided audio tou
 r to reveal the drama etched into the DCU Center\, the strange magic cling
 ing to Burnside Fountain\, and the faded glories of Worcester Memorial Aud
 itorium. Uncover secrets in spots often hurried past and hear tales most v
 isitors never imagine. Why did a crowd once swarm these steps in desperate
  protest? What secrets echo after midnight around Turtle Boy’s pedestal?
  What scandal unraveled inside the Auditorium’s grand halls over a centu
 ry ago? Stride through echoes of parades and protests\, scandals and celeb
 rations. Every corner holds a revelation and every story lets you see Worc
 ester through new eyes. Start your journey and meet the city’s mysteries
  where they stand-turtle\, stone\, and memory intertwined.\n\nSources: Dis
 cover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org
 /event/audatours-worcester-audio-tour%3a-statues-spires-%26-civic-stories-
 unveiled/29278/
LOCATION:St. John's Catholic Church (Worcester\, Massachusetts)\, 44 Templ
 e St\, Worcester\, MA\, 01604
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/audatours-worcester-audio-tour
 %3a-statues-spires-%26-civic-stories-unveiled/29278/
END:VEVENT
