  about 4 centuries of Harvard history\, including stories about the 7 pres
 idents who went to Harvard. The Hahvahd Tour: Harvard student guides greet
  you right in Harvard Square. The tour is scripted to be an entertaining\,
  theatrical experience - you'll have fun learning about Harvard! Our tours
  are led in English. For those who do not speak English we also provide co
 mplimentary written translations in French\, Spanish\, German\, Italian\, 
 Simplified Chinese\, Korean\, and Portuguese which allow guests to read al
 ong during the tour. Harvard Main Tour Stops Include: Harvard Yard - inclu
 ding Old Yard and New Yard Historic Buildings - Memorial Hall\, Sever Hall
 \, The Widener Library and the Harvard Lampoon The famous John Harvard Sta
 tue Surrounding Neighborhood of Harvard Square - including the Plaza\, Win
 throp Park and Mt. Auburn Street Tour Themes Include: Harvard History - in
 cluding the untold stories and lore of Harvard University Harvard Culture 
 - stories and tips from current students about what it's like to live and 
 study at Harvard Famous Harvardians - learn about the most famous people t
 o attend Harvard Harvard Tour Guides: Tour guides are current Harvard unde
 rgraduate students\, graduate students and Harvard alumni.\n\nSources: Mee
 t Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/tour-of-harvard/398
 15/
