SUMMARY:Portraits Gallery & History of the Hall A Mechanics Hall Guided To
 ur
DTSTART:20260716T000000
DTEND:20270617T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:df2594ef88881edf679eed982c8a27@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided tour of Mechanics Hall\, Worcester’s tr
 easured landmark and architectural gem. Internationally recognized for its
  superb acoustics and breathtaking beauty\, Mechanics Hall is one of the w
 orld’s great concert halls and a premier venue for performances\, record
 ings\, weddings\, business events\, and more. As part of this special tour
 \, Mechanics Hall Principal Organist Peter Krasinski will provide a live d
 emonstration and discussion on The Worcester Organ\, the Hall’s historic
  tracker pipe organ\, known as The Hook Organ. Built in 1864\, this magnif
 icent instrument remains one of the finest surviving examples of its kind.
  Experience its power and grandeur as Peter Krasinski shares insights into
  its history\, mechanics\, and breathtaking sound. Open to the Public – 
 Limited Availability Admission: $10 FREE for Mechanics Hall Members\n\nSou
 rces: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercent
 ralma.org/event/portraits-gallery-%26-history-of-the-hall-a-mechanics-hall
 -guided-tour/30389/
LOCATION:Mechanics Hall\, 321 Main St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/portraits-gallery-%26-history-
 of-the-hall-a-mechanics-hall-guided-tour/30389/
