BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alfonso Ossorio: Line and Lineage
DTSTART:20261023T000000
DTEND:20270411T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:5755e3786166ae75f5640f32aa28eb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Trace the artistic lineage of Alfonso Ossorio through a body o
 f works that resonates across generations. Through a focused selection of 
 works and archival materials\, Alfonso Ossorio: Line and Lineage explores 
 the recurrent subjects\, material experimentation\, and development of lin
 e in prints\, drawings\, and wax-resist paintings by Alfonso Ossorio (1916
 –1990). Born in the Philippines\, Ossorio studied art history at Harvard
  and shortly after moved to New York City\, becoming an influential figure
  in the post–World War II American avant-garde. Showcasing works that ch
 art both continuities and innovations across his six-decade practice\, the
  exhibition positions Ossorio in dialogue with the artists he influenced\,
  learned from\, and inspired. The exhibition is organized in conjunction w
 ith Knowledge Is Myth: Chimeric Continuities (October 1–December 13\, 20
 26) at the neighboring Carpenter Center for the Visual Arts. Works by Osso
 rio as well as by Enzo Camacho and Ami Lien\, a contemporary artist duo wh
 o engage with the continuing influence of a larger-than-life church mural 
 that Ossorio completed in the Philippines\, appear in both exhibitions. Pr
 ogramming\, including talks led by exhibition curators\, will be hosted by
  both the Harvard Art Museums and the Carpenter Center throughout the run 
 of the exhibitions. LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https:
 //www.meetboston.com/event/alfonso-ossorio%3a-line-and-lineage/94019/
LOCATION:Harvard Art Museums\, Harvard Art Museums 32 Quincy Street\, Camb
 ridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/alfonso-ossorio%3a-line-and-lineage/9
 4019/
END:VEVENT
