DESCRIPTION:The Paul S. Russell\, MD Museum of Medical History and Innovat
 ion at Massachusetts General Hospital invites you to its next hybrid lectu
 re. "Deliberate Practice: What Musicians\, Athletes\, and Others Can Teach
  Us About Expertise" will be presented by Keith Baker\, MD\, PhD\, HMS Pro
 fessor of Clinical Anaesthesia on Tuesday\, November 10 from 6 to 7 pm. We
  welcome you to attend in person at 2 North Grove Street or virtually thro
 ugh Zoom. Anesthesiologist and educator Keith Baker has spent decades comp
 iling research about how health care professionals and others become exper
 ts. Whereas quantity of practice matters\, so does quality\, as Baker will
  explain\, providing tips for clinicians--and the rest of us. To register 
 for this event (either in person or virtually)\, click here. A Zoom link w
 ill be sent to all attendees closer to the event through your Eventbrite r
