BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Awareness in Sound
DTSTART:20261111T000000
DTEND:20261111T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:f604dbe58b1e0202ed559dce4537c9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Awareness in Sound is an immersive 45–60 minute immersive an
 d participatory auditory workshop that centers the healing and grounding p
 ower of mindful listening. In a world filled with constant noise\, speed\,
  and pressure\, this session offers space to pause\, breathe\, and reconne
 ct with one’s internal landscape. During the session\, participants will
  be given the space to become more aware of themselves and engage in visua
 lization work\, activating their imagination to have a more internalized s
 ense of the feeling and sensation responses to sound. As the workshop prog
 resses\, participants explore sensory awareness and experiment with guided
  improvisation. The workshop concludes with closing reflections and practi
 cal take-aways for integrating mindful listening into everyday life. Led b
 y COOS Teaching Artist Matt Williams II\, this workshop is ideal for stude
 nts\, community groups\, arts organizations\, workplaces\, and anyone seek
 ing new tools for self-care\, creativity\, and internal grounding. Accessi
 bility: Piano Craft Gallery's front entrance on Tremont Street has stairs 
 leading down into gallery\, with handicap accessible entrance as needed at
  apartment entrance. Once in the gallery\, it's a singular-level space wit
 h two accessible bathrooms for public use. Public Transit: Orangeline (Mas
 sachusetts Ave.)\, #1 Bus (Massachusetts Ave. at Tremont St.)\, #43 Bus (T
 remont St. at Northapmpton St.)\, Greenline (Symphony) Parking: Unmetered 
 street parking on Tremont St.\, Camden St.\, Columbus Ave.\, & Massachuset
 ts Ave. REASONABLE ACCOMMODATION REQUESTS: Castle of our Skins does not di
 scriminate on the basis of disability\, and is committed to providing acce
 ssible programs and events to facilitate participation. A guest or outside
  organization must notify Castle of our Skins of any request for an accomm
 odation in advance of the event (ideally 2-3 weeks before). Late accommoda
 tion requests\, or requests made the day of the event\, may not be possibl
 e to provide. Please send requests to info@castleskins.org. MORE INFO HERE
 \n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/awa
 reness-in-sound/93282/
LOCATION:Piano Craft Gallery\, Piano Craft Gallery 793 Tremont St.\, Bosto
 n\, MA\, 02118
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/awareness-in-sound/93282/
END:VEVENT
