BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Veterans Day Special Anniversary Walking Tour
DTSTART:20261111T000000
DTEND:20261111T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:c31878a7543930052d7ae2bc2fe65c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Hub Town Tours for a special Veterans Day tour\, commemor
 ating the historic contributions of the Massachusetts 54th Regiment. The f
 irst Black regiment from the North enlisted troops from Boston and around 
 the state\, and was led by Col. Robert Gould Shaw\, son of local abolition
 ists. This 2.5-hour walking tour explores sites along the Black Heritage T
 rail in Boston's Beacon Hill neighborhood\, including abolitionist landmar
 ks such as the African Meeting House and the Robert Gould Shaw / 54th MA M
 emorial. Along the way\, we dive deeply into the years before the U.S. Civ
 il War as 19th-century Bostonians grappled with the institution of slavery
  and demanded an end to racial injustice across their young nation.\n\nSou
 rces: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/veterans-d
 ay-special-anniversary-walking-tour/88880/
LOCATION:Soldiers & Sailors Monument\, Boston Common\, Soldiers & Sailors 
 Monument\, Boston Common\, Boston\, MA\, 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/veterans-day-special-anniversary-walk
 ing-tour/88880/
END:VEVENT
