BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cape Ann Shakespeare Troupe presents Laugh Out Loud
DTSTART:20261112T193000
DTEND:20261112T213000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:028adefad24d0c1858d85574d7d7ee@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Cape Ann Shakespeare Troupe (CAST) kicks off its 2026-27 seaso
 n with Laugh Out Loud. Shakespeare’s quote “Prepare for mirth\, for mi
 rth becomes a feast.” aptly describes this feast of modern one-act comed
 ies: Base Model Man and Who Ate the Cheetos? by Kevin Perrin of the Glouce
 ster Writers Center\, and Black Comedy by Peter Shaffer. Base Model Man\, 
 directed by Alexis Armstrong\, imagines a dealership where a woman shops f
 or the perfect man with available upgrades such as “willing to share hou
 sework” and “actually listens”. Directed by Billy Lewand\, Who Ate t
 he Cheetos? is an eight minute comedy in which a simple family mystery eru
 pts into a full-blown courtroom style confrontation a la A Few Good Men. I
 n the classic farce Black Comedy\, directed by Mark Efinger\, a young arti
 st and his fiancée secretly furnish their apartment with a neighbor’s e
 xpensive antiques before meeting her intimidating military father. When th
 e electricity fails and unexpected guests arrive – a suspicious neighbor
 \, a nervous spinster\, a talkative electrician\, and an old girlfriend—
 the comic chaos escalates. Performing from November 5th-8th and 12th-15th
 \, all performances are at The Natti-Willsky Performance Center: Home of G
 loucester Stage Company\, 267 East Main Street\, Gloucester. Showtimes are
  Thursdays-Saturdays at 7:30pm and Sundays at 3:00pm. Tickets can be purch
 ased online or by calling the box office at 978-281-4433.\n\nSources: Nort
 h of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/cape-ann-shakespe
 are-troupe-presents-laugh-out-loud/2026-11-12/
LOCATION:Natti-Willsky Performance Center: Home of Gloucester Stage Compan
 y\, 267 East Main St.\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/cape-ann-shakespeare-troupe-presents-l
 augh-out-loud/2026-11-12/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club 321 featuring Mark Mandeville & Raianne Richards
DTSTART:20261112T000000
DTEND:20261112T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:46ec3ea6a8c7f7e855eed908dd9873@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Artist: Mark Mandeville & Raianne Richards Join us at Club 321
  for an evening of heartfelt storytelling\, rich harmonies\, and authentic
  folk/Americana music with Mark & Raianne. Returning after a packed-house 
 performance last year\, this beloved husband-and-wife duo brings back thei
 r unmistakable vocal blend and down-to-earth stage presence for another in
 timate night at Club 321. Known for their rich harmonies and poetic songwr
 iting\, Mark & Raianne weave together original music and traditional acous
 tic instrumentation—including guitar\, mandolin\, banjo\, harmonica\, uk
 ulele\, clarinet\, and penny whistle—to create a sound that is both inti
 mate and expansive. With more than seventeen albums recorded in their firs
 t decade together and extensive touring throughout the U.S. and Canada\, t
 heir performances balance thoughtful\, poetic songwriting with moments of 
 humor\, connection\, and community. Deeply rooted in Central Massachusetts
 \, the duo are also founders of the Massachusetts Walking Tour\, an annual
  initiative that combines outdoor exploration with free community concerts
  to celebrate local green spaces and connection through music. This is a p
 erfect Club 321 evening for listeners who value storytelling\, acoustic be
 auty\, and music that feels close to home. Experience a different side of 
 Mechanics Hall\, in our intimate Washburn Hall\, transformed one Thursday 
 night a month into your favorite club. Come sip handcrafted drinks from ou
 r full bar\, and enjoy cabaret-style seating. An unforgettable evening in 
 the heart of downtown Worcester! ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Tickets: $30 Mecha
 nics Hall Members: 10% discount off single ticket Time: Doors 6:15pm | Sho
 w 7:00pm Cash bar and refreshments available for purchase\n\nSources: Disc
 over Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/
 event/club-321-featuring-mark-mandeville-%26-raianne-richards/30395/
LOCATION:Mechanics Hall\, 321 Main St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/club-321-featuring-mark-mandev
 ille-%26-raianne-richards/30395/
END:VEVENT
