SUMMARY:Kennedy's Only Hero
DTSTART:20261112T000000
DTEND:20261112T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:ed418b154ab96513199147209c6440@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Joel Nelson is a British historian and author whose work focus
 es on political history and influential figures. He is a former Kennedy Sc
 holar and has served as an assistant editor at Foreign Affairs. He studied
  at Oxford and Harvard Universities. His debut book\, Kennedy’s Only Her
 o\, highlights the impact of Winston Churchill on John F. Kennedy. The boo
 k examines the profound influence Winston Churchill had on John F. Kennedy
 \, detailing how Kennedy’s early admiration for Churchill shaped his pol
 itical philosophy\, campaign strategies\, and approach to international re
 lations. The work draws on unpublished archival material to provide new in
 sights into the relationship between these two historical figures. Althoug
 h Kennedy’s Only Hero focuses on Churchill’s impact\, the Kennedys the
 mselves shared a special connection with Falmouth. JFK and Jacqueline Kenn
 edy often visited The Antiquarian\, an antique shop on Palmer Avenue\, whe
 re they admired a distinctive pink West Falmouth granite stone. Jacqueline
  later recalled that stone when collaborating with architect John Carl War
 necke on the design of the president’s gravesite and eternal flame at Ar
 lington National Cemetery. The family also maintained close ties with Falm
 outh interior designer Robert Luddington\, who exchanged design sketches a
 nd handwritten correspondence with Jackie and Rose Kennedy for many years.
  Tickets: $20 Non-Members\, $10 Museums on the Green Members Register Here
 \n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/
 event/kennedys-only-hero/52636/
LOCATION:Falmouth Museums on the Green\, 55 & 65 Palmer Avenue\, Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/kennedys-only-hero/52636/
END:VEVENT
