BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Winter Birds of Nantucket Sound
DTSTART:20261112T000000
DTEND:20261112T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:daad1fa3be40684f6133ae940251b1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:For birdwatchers\, bird lovers\, and nature lovers\, winter ma
 y be the Cape’s most exciting season of all. Join the Alliance to Protec
 t Nantucket Sound for a fascinating ACONS ( A Celebration of Nantucket Sou
 nd ) webinar with prominent naturalist and educator John Hanlon as we expl
 ore the remarkable winter bird species that migrate south each year to Cap
 e Cod\, the Islands\, and Nantucket Sound. Just in time for the winter mon
 ths ahead! From colorful waterfowl and diving ducks to loons\, grebes\, an
 d other coastal birds\, the Cape & islands become a seasonal refuge for wi
 ldlife that breeds far to the north. As John puts it\, “Winter on the Ca
 pe is like Florida for them!” Register for free at: https://tinyurl.com/
 SOS-WinterBirds This engaging presentation will introduce viewers to the b
 irds that transform our shores and waters during the colder months\, while
  also offering insight into the habitats and ecosystems that make Nantucke
 t Sound such an important winter sanctuary. Whether you’re an experience
 d birder\, a casual nature lover\, or simply curious about the wildlife th
 at arrives with the winter season\, this lively and educational webinar wi
 ll deepen your appreciation for the natural wonders of Nantucket Sound—j
 ust in time for winter on the Cape. About John Hanlon: A longtime naturali
 st educator and outreach ranger affiliated with the Cape Cod National Seas
 hore\, John Hanlon has dedicated his career to connecting people with the 
 natural world through birding walks\, educational programs\, and community
  outreach across Cape Cod. His work with the National Park Service\, Mashp
 ee Wampanoag Tribe\, and Cape Cod Community College has helped make enviro
 nmental education more accessible and inclusive throughout the region.\n\n
 Sources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/even
 t/winter-birds-of-nantucket-sound/52460/
LOCATION:Alliance to Protect Nantucket Sound\, Inc\, 4 Barnstable Road\, H
 yannis\, MA\, 02601
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/winter-birds-of-nantucket-sound/5
 2460/
END:VEVENT
