BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261112T111500
DTEND:20261112T161500
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:8cd770a0ab482b605bce08abded234@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-11-12/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 1-12/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening of Piano Music by Candlelight
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261113T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:f432a728e3662009250478e1945068@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into an unforgettable evening where music and candlelight
  create an atmosphere of warmth\, beauty\, and romance. Surrounded by the 
 soft glow of hundreds of candles\, you'll experience a carefully curated p
 rogram featuring timeless classical masterpieces\, beloved film scores\, a
 nd modern love songs performed with elegance and artistry. Whether you're 
 planning a date night\, celebrating a special occasion\, or simply looking
  for a peaceful escape\, this intimate concert offers a chance to slow dow
 n\, savor the moment and be inspired by the beauty of live music. Your tic
 ket includes desserts and non-alcoholic drinks\, making it the perfect eve
 ning to relax\, indulge\, and enjoy an enchanting night out. About Jonatha
 n Weir: Jonathan is a Cape Cod-based pianist\, vocalist\, composer\, and e
 ducator with a passion for creating meaningful musical experiences. A grad
 uate of the University of Hartford's Hartt School\, where he earned a Bach
 elor of Music in Piano Performance and Composition\, Jonathan brings toget
 her the artistry of classical piano with the warmth and accessibility of c
 ontemporary favorites. Whether performing for weddings\, concerts\, or pri
 vate events\, his goal is simple: to create moments of beauty\, connection
 \, and lasting memories through music. DOORS @ 6:30 PM | MUSIC BEGINS @ 7:
 00 PM\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber
 .org/event/an-evening-of-piano-music-by-candlelight/52667/
LOCATION:Thacher Hall\, 266 Route 6A P.O. Box 237\, Yarmouth Port\, MA\, 0
 2675
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/an-evening-of-piano-music-by-cand
 lelight/52667/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BAILEN
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261113T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:2bf23ca24d70c4d9404729e22a4020@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:BAILEN is a songwriting-forward indie pop/folk-rock band that 
 has captivated audiences with its musical dynamism and the three-part "blo
 od harmony" of siblings Julia (guitar)\, Daniel (bass)\, and David (drums)
 . The trio was raised in New York City by two freelance classical musician
 s who steeped them in rock 'n' roll and Brahms. Their close familial bond 
 is evident in their tight-knit musical arrangements and rich\, emotive har
 monies. Currently\, BAILEN is preparing to release its third full-length a
 lbum\, which the band engineered and produced with collaborators Jake Sinc
 lair (Panic! At the Disco)\, Riccardo Damian (Sampha)\, and Chris Tabron (
 the Strokes). The band is excited to release the record fully independentl
 y.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/b
 ailen/91543/
LOCATION:The Red Room at Cafe 939\, 939 Boylston St\, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/bailen/91543/
END:VEVENT
