DESCRIPTION:This November\, we're heading to the Worcester Idea Lab to tal
 k small business\, entrepreneurship\, and resources to help businesses thr
 ive Downtown. Special guest Tom Herald\, Regional Director of the Massachu
 setts Small Business Development Center (SBDC) at Clark University\, will 
 share insights into the SBDC's work and resources for entrepreneurs. If yo
 u own a business\, dream of starting one\, or simply want to connect with 
 others invested in Downtown's success\, we hope you'll join us. Plus\, enj
 oy complimentary breakfast & coffee from one of Downtown's newest business
 es: Golden Grain Artisanal Bread! Whether you’ve been to every Downtown 
 Worcester Community Meeting to date or you’ve never joined us before\, t
 his is your invitation. Come explore. Meet someone new. Learn something ne
 w about Downtown. Bring a friend or colleague. Downtown Worcester Communit
 y Meetings are free and open to everyone. Register by Thursday\, November 
 12 at: https://lp.constantcontactpages.com/ev/reg/cqug233 We’d love to s
