BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Glass Etching Workshop
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261216T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:be9775aab63976b354aae5ad1e5c63@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Discover the art of glass etching in this hands-on creative wo
 rkshop! Guests will design and tape their own custom pattern onto a glass 
 piece of their choice—options may include a wine glass\, pint glass\, or
  small dish. Once your design is in place\, your instructor will carefully
  sandblast the piece\, revealing a beautifully etched version of your artw
 ork. This beginner-friendly experience covers the basics of glass etching 
 while giving you the freedom to create something uniquely yours. Whether y
 ou design a simple pattern\, monogram\, or decorative motif\, you’ll lea
 ve with a gorgeous\, functional piece that’s perfect for your kitchen or
  as a personalized gift. No prior experience is needed\; just bring your c
 reativity and enjoy the process of transforming everyday glass into a cust
 om work of art! Ticket covers one piece\; guests may add on an additional 
 piece day of for $25 if they wish.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent pag
 e: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/glass-etching-workshop/52621/
LOCATION:Sandwich Glass Museum\, 129 Main Street\, Sandwich\, MA\, 02563
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/glass-etching-workshop/52621/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Handmade Butter
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261113T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:88e88656c68963bfb7e79ea0c915fb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Teens ages 12-18 are invited to the Burncoat Branch to learn h
 ow to handmake butter while supplies last! Mix in seasonings and spices fo
