BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:HUB History Live Podcast
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261113T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:7649b88b7d6ee2007215319db5bf91@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The popular podcast HUB History\, hosted by Jake Sconyers\, is
  celebrating its 10th anniversary with a live episode at the Old North Chu
 rch! The episode\, a discussion with historians Lori Rogers-Stokes and Jon
 athan Chu\, will focus on the Puritan legacy that still shapes Boston and 
 New England today. Have you ever wondered how Massachusetts went from the 
 stern Puritanism of Increase Mather to the hopeful liberalism of Mike Duka
 kis? From the most conservative British North American colony to the most 
 progressive American state? Despite their stern and unbending reputation\,
  17th century Puritans saw themselves as progressive reformers committed t
 o continuous learning and adaptation\, and the vast woodlands of New Engla
 nd would be the garden where the seeds of a new culture could grow unimped
 ed by the religious and governmental constraints of Europe. Jake\, Lori\, 
 and Jonathan will examine how the Puritans created our modern values of un
 iversal literacy and education\, direct participation in government\, and 
 (eventually) separation of church and state. LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Meet B
 oston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/hub-history-live-podca
 st/93986/
LOCATION:Old North Church & Historic Site\, Old North Church & Historic Si
 te 193 Salem Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02113
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/hub-history-live-podcast/93986/
END:VEVENT
