BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MIT Festival Jazz Ensemble
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261113T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:87478db3b01b334ccc1951972e844d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the MIT Festival Jazz Ensemble and special guest tromboni
 st Elliot Mason for the 19th annual celebration of Herb Pomeroy (1930-2007
 )\, “the father of jazz at MIT.” This concert includes music of Elling
 ton\, Coltrane\, Chick Corea\, Miguel Zenón\, and others. Throughout his 
 career\, he has performed with many of jazz’ most celebrated ensembles\,
  including the Count Basie Orchestra\, the Mingus Big Band\, the Maria Sch
 neider Orchestra\, Maynard Ferguson’s Big Bop Nouveau\, and the Toshiko 
 Akiyoshi Orchestra. As a featured performer and collaborator\, Mason has s
 hared the stage with an extraordinary range of artists\, including Paul Si
 mon\, Wayne Shorter\, Branford Marsalis\, Chick Corea\, Kenny Garrett\, Bo
 bby Hutcherson\, Ahmad Jamal\, Chucho Valdés\, Chano Domínguez\, Chris P
 otter\, Randy Brecker\, Joe Lovano\, Carl Fontana\, and Bill Watrous. His 
 distinctive musical voice\, technical mastery\, and fearless innovative im
 provisation have made Mason one of the most influential jazz trombonists o
 f his generation. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent 
 page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/mit-festival-jazz-ensemble/94133/
LOCATION:Thomas Tull Concert Hall\, Thomas Tull Concert Hall 201 Amherst S
 treet\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02139
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/mit-festival-jazz-ensemble/94133/
END:VEVENT
