BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thanksgiving Stories
DTSTART:20261113T000000
DTEND:20261113T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:fcbdd6fdd2651c00af64c7dbed1a14@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a reading of Keepunumuk: Weeȃchumun's Thanksgivin
 g Story. Written and illustrated by four Indigenous creators\, this beauti
 ful picture book honors the history and tradition that surround the story 
 of the first Thanksgiving. Discover the first Thanksgiving through Wampano
 ag eyes\, as the Native Americans teach the Pilgrims to grow the three sis
 ters — corn\, beans\, and squash — for a successful harvest. This fall
  favorite is written by Danielle Greendeer (Mashpee Wampanoag)\, Anthony P
 erry (Chickasaw) and Alexis Bunten (Unangan/Yup’ik) and beautifully illu
 strated by Garry Meeches Sr. (Anishinaabe). After the story\, be sure to c
 heck out the works by past and present Native American artists on view in 
 On This Ground: Being and Belonging in America. Designed for children (5 a
 nd under) and their caregivers\, PEM Pals aims to engage and excite all of
  the senses through books\, movement\, music\, art and hands-on activities
 . Held on the first Friday of the month at 10:30 am. LEARN MORE / GET TICK
 ETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/
 thanksgiving-stories/93921/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, Peabody Essex Museum 161 Essex Street\, Sa
 lem\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/thanksgiving-stories/93921/
END:VEVENT
