 ns and support military families. Admission is free for both games. The Be
 acons will open the weekend on Friday\, Nov. 13\, at 7 p.m. against New En
 gland College. A special guest will drop the puck at Friday night’s game
 \, Boston Police Commissioner Michael A. Cox. The Beacons will return to t
 he ice Saturday\, Nov. 14\, at 4 p.m. to face Plymouth State University. B
  oth games will be played at the Edward T. Barry Ice Rink in the Clark Ath
 letic Center on the UMass Boston campus (100 William T Morrissey Blvd\, Bo
 ston\, MA\, 02125). Military Appreciation Weekend activities will include 
 Veteran recognition\, special guest puck drop\, chuck-a-puck\, prize givea
 ways\, an opportunity to meet Bobby the Beacon and more. Throughout the tw
 o-day event\, volunteers from Operation Shower will collect donations to s
 upport the nonprofit organization and its work with military families. LEA
