BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gauri B
DTSTART:20261115T000000
DTEND:20261115T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:44556649384767863ee1c8bea31435@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Gauri has headlined top tier comedy clubs and festivals around
  the world\, from Leicester Square Theater in London to WUK in Vienna\, to
  the Melbourne International Comedy Festival in Australia. Her clips have 
 amassed hundreds of millions of views on social media and gained her a glo
 bal following. Gauri enjoys tackling morbid subjects and infusing them wit
 h hard hitting punchlines\, which she delivers with a natural charisma. Fe
 arless and unabashed\, Gauri draws material from politics and society\, we
 aving personal stories with incisive jokes. And when it comes to crowd wor
 k and interacting with the audience\, she is undoubtedly in a league of he
 r own.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/eve
 nt/gauri-b/93347/
LOCATION:City Winery Boston\, 80 Beverly Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02128
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/gauri-b/93347/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ghostlight on the Fifth: A Staged Reading
DTSTART:20261115T000000
DTEND:20261115T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:4e57585a162f3c71685e63852b4a64@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Studio Theatre Worcester is proud to present a staged reading 
 of Ghostlight on the Fifth on November 15th at 6:00pm. This tremendous new
  work by playwright Carlos Fruzzetti is in development as part of our Firs
 t Stages initiative. This public-facing staged reading\, directed by Jada 
 Lawyer\, is a crucial checkpoint in this play's development as it provides
  the playwright with insights from the audience perspective. We also invit
 e you to join us following the reading for a brief 30min feedback session
 \, moderated by our Producer and Dramaturg\, Amanda Tafeen. SYNOPSIS It’
 s midnight on the fifth of April in a rehearsal space they call Delirium. 
 Ghostlight is a young\, ambitious rock band that’s taken residence here.
  Tonight\, they’re on the verge of collapse. One of them is leaving. One
  of them is spiraling. One can’t play his guitar anymore. Through the ni
 ght\, the space oscillates back and forth between the murmurings\, melodie
 s\, and memories of this haunted band as they attempt to overcome their st
 ruggles. When the sun rises\, we’re left to wonder what is real\, what i
 s memory\, what is neither masked as both\, and what’s the difference?\n
 \nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discove
 rcentralma.org/event/ghostlight-on-the-fifth%3a-a-staged-reading/31080/
LOCATION:WCUW Radio Front Room\, 910 Main Street\, Worcester\, MA\, 01610
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/ghostlight-on-the-fifth%3a-a-s
 taged-reading/31080/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Growing Together: Natural Fall/Winter Decorations from the Garden
DTSTART:20261115T100000
DTEND:20261115T120000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:efa7fcdb8806655772c0900b91dfa0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Bring the garden’s beauty indoors with this hands-on worksho
 p focused on creating beautiful winter decorations using natural materials
 . Participants will explore how to gather and preserve seasonal branches\,
  evergreens\, dried flowers\, seed heads\, berries\, grasses\, and other g
 arden treasures to create festive botanical accents for the home. This cla
 ss celebrates the textures\, colors\, and forms of the fall/winter garden 
 while offering creative\, sustainable alternatives to store-bought decorat
 ions. Growing Together is a hands-on gardening series created in collabora
 tion with Arianna Iappini of Birch Arbor Gardens. Designed for gardeners o
 f all experience levels\, this series invites participants to learn\, conn
 ect\, and cultivate alongside one another through the seasons. Each sessio
 n blends practical instruction with thoughtful conversation\, exploring su
 stainable gardening practices\, seasonal rhythms\, and the deeper relation
 ships between plants\, place\, and people. Rooted in community and shared 
 knowledge\, Growing Together offers a welcoming space to grow skills\, con
 fidence\, and connection in the historic gardens. Space is limited—pre-r
 egistration is required for this event. This program is rain or shine! In 
 the event of cancellation\, you will be notified via the email address you
  used to register and refunded in full within 14 business days. Tickets ar
 e non-transferable and non-refundable. Membership: To locate information a
 bout your Membership\, including Member ID\, expiration date\, and more pl
 ease visit: https://explore.thetrustees.org/manage. Tickets: To look up yo
 ur tickets or re-send an email confirmation\, please visit: https://explor
 e.thetrustees.org/order-lookup.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: h
 ttps://northofboston.org/event/growing-together-natural-fall-winter-decora
 tions-from-the-garden/
LOCATION:Stevens-Coolidge House &amp\; Gardens\, 153 Chickering Road\, Nor
 th Andover\, MA\, 01845
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/growing-together-natural-fall-winter-d
 ecorations-from-the-garden/
END:VEVENT
