UID:46ea431cd66477760e07ff2395da48@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Ekep Nkwelle is a force in today’s jazz scene\, with a journ
 ey from Washington\, DC\, to New York City. She refined her talents at Duk
 e Ellington School of the Arts\, Howard University\, and The Juilliard Sch
 ool. “Nkwelle is a rising star of her own.” –All About Jazz Her capt
 ivating voice has earned her collaborations with jazz legends like Wynton 
 Marsalis\, Dianne Reeves\, Dee Dee Bridgewater\, Cyrus Chestnut\, and the 
 late Russell Malone. She has also performed on renowned stages including S
 FJAZZ\, NPR’s Tiny Desk Concert\, Marians Jazzroom\, and the Umbria Jazz
  Festival. In 2023\, she received the Juilliard Career Advancement Grant\,
  nominated by Marsalis\, highlighting her artistry. Beyond performing\, Ek
 ep supports influential arts organizations including The National Jazz Mus
 eum in Harlem and Jazz Houston\, and she is one of Jazz at Lincoln Center
 ’s latest rising stars.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https:/
 /northofboston.org/event/ekep-nkwelle/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/ekep-nkwelle/
END:VEVENT
