BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Christian Sands
DTSTART:20261129T170000
DTEND:20261129T190000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:00fbc2ac6cddb5863ad0bdf71f00fc@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Jazz history is filled with stirring torch songs and ballads 
 — brilliant expressions of suffering after love has gone awry. The jazz 
 record shelf even contains some classic album-long explorations of melanch
 oly. But it’s hard to find precedent in pianist Christian Sands’ new E
 mbracing Dawn\, his fifth full-length effort for Mack Avenue Records. Sand
 s’ LP is nothing less than a cinematic narration of the stages of grief
 \, crafted by one of jazz’s finest young composers. It’s a “breakup 
 record\,” to be sure — composed while Sands was experiencing the hurt 
 that only a sudden absence of love can deliver — but it’s so much more
 . In its thoughtfully assembled nine tracks are a group therapy session\, 
 a guide to healing\, and an understanding that Sands’ deeply personal an
 gst could apply to any person who has lost a partner\, a job\, a loved one
 \, an opportunity\, the list goes on. In other words\, Embracing Dawn is f
 or everyone. “I actually tried not to write this record\,” Sands says 
 with a laugh. “It was painful. I was going through heartbreak\, and I di
 dn’t know what to do — and so I decided to put it all into music. But 
 I knew I wasn’t alone in this feeling. So why not create a safe space fo
 r people to go when they’re having this feeling\, when they’re having 
 these thoughts or questions?” Embracing Dawn trails 2023’s acclaimed C
 hristmas Stories and 2020’s GRAMMY-nominated Be Water. Following that al
 bum’s release\, the New York Times commented\, “Equipped with a crisp 
 but forceful touch\, he seems always to be flowing in new directions\, int
 egrating elements of prog rock\, gospel and Western classical into a forwa
 rd-tumbling jazz conception.” Embracing Dawn furthers Sands’ uniquely 
 cultivated jazz language\, where agile post-bop meets soulful bluesy tinge
 s and gorgeous swells of strings. Sands’ love of classical orchestration
 \, he explains\, is rooted in his lifelong obsession with film. Ultimately
 \, Sands’ sound and philosophy are informed by two of his most essential
  mentors: bass maestro Christian McBride\, who\, as Sands’ longtime empl
 oyer\, taught him the importance of always being yourself\; and the late p
 iano legend Dr. Billy Taylor\, who stressed how crucial it is to connect j
 azz to a wide-ranging audience. “I want Embracing Dawn to be something y
 ou gravitate toward because of the story\,” Sands says.\n\nSources: Nort
 h of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/christian-sands-2
 /
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/christian-sands-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deck the Halls at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261129T090000
DTEND:20261129T153000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:c0517888591faccd10582433b90516@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Holiday Season as we proudly present our 
 8th annual holiday celebration\, Deck the Halls\, a Museum-wide holiday in
 stallation! Travel back in time to a castle filled with candlelight and lu
 sh\, opulent textures inspired by the great medieval and Renaissance castl
 es of Europe. We are delighted to partner again with Elaine Quinn Interior
 s\, a boutique residential interior design firm based in Manchester-by-the
 -Sea\, to bring heightened inspiration and artistry to this year’s museu
 m-wide holiday installation. Abundant greenery and sumptuous layers of dé
 cor create a richly immersive seasonal experience throughout the Museum. W
 ander through rooms adorned with white birch and Christmas trees\, sparkli
 ng fairy lights\, hydrangea-lace garlands\, and elegant bows\, with each s
 pace transformed by its own unique holiday theme. This celebration also em
 braces the traditions of Hanukkah\, with two beautifully displayed menorah
 s adding their own warm glow to the Museum’s festive splendor. From natu
 re’s bounty of fruits and greenery to the warm glow of candlelight\, eve
 ry detail creates a feast for the senses. Along the way\, encounter a roya
 l guard of nutcrackers\, a gingerbread house replica of the Museum\, and p
 layful elves and gnomes up to mischief\, adding a touch of whimsy for litt
 le ones. In addition to the holiday installation\, guests can enjoy the te
 mporary exhibition\, “Brave-Too-Much”: The Legend of John Coffee Hays.
  Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to fully experience the h
 oliday installation and exhibition Extended Tuesday and Thursday Tour Hour
 s: New this year\, visitors can enjoy extended hours on Tuesdays and Thurs
 days\, with last entry at 7:15 p.m. These extended guided and self-guided 
 tour hours offer greater opportunities to experience the Museum after dark
 \, when holiday décor glows with flickering candlelight and twinkling lig
 hts. Upon arrival\, visitors will discover the path and outdoor Courtyard
 \, arches and towers aglow with festive holiday lighting\, creating a trul
 y magical seasonal atmosphere. Visitors will have more time to explore the
  Museum’s holiday decorations and experience the beauty of this historic
  site after dark. Admission pricing varies\, please visit our website for 
 accurate pricing. Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to take 
 in the full holiday grandeur. Museum member benefits apply.\n\nSources: No
 rth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-
 at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-11-29/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-at-hammond-castle-museu
 m/2026-11-29/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gloucester Film Release of The Networks: Art + Fishing + Community
DTSTART:20261129T180000
DTEND:20261129T200000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:89f9d4fbcbc38fa7b1ca0190ac6f48@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:13+\, Under 18 must be accompanied by an adult “The NetWorks
 : Art + Fishing + Community” will have its US premiere and release celeb
 rations this November 2026. Film Director and Producer Ken Kinna of B-Roll
  Films will host a film lunch and release party at the Cut on Nov 29th. Th
 e event will feature Q&A with the main characters and supporting organizat
 ions\, including: Erika Senft Miller\, Ann Molloy\, Joe Sanfilippo and Jam
 es Tarantino. The film is about an art project initiated by Manship Artist
 s Residency and an international multi-sensory artist (Senft Miller) comin
 g from Vermont with a team of artists to work with local Gloucester fisher
 men and local artists to create an immersive art installation on the harbo
 r of Gloucester\, Massachusetts. The film celebrates this combined communi
 ty effort and also introduces us to some of our fishermen and takes up som
 e of the topics confronting the fishing industry today. The film is dedica
 ted to the crew of the F/V Lilly Jean. This film was recently honored with
  three film awards in Sicily\, this past August\, including: Best Cultural
  Film\, Best Director\, and Best Feature Documentary inspiring a trip to S
 icily by some of the contributors to The NetWorks public art project who a
 re featured in the film\, inspiring and renewed connection to the fishing 
 and cultural heritage of Gloucester. Kinna and Raynolds hope these events 
 will bring together many of those involved and invite new opportunities fo
 r communication around the themes of fishing\, the arts\, and community. I
 t is clear that the heritage is great but it is also clear that more commu
 nication and action is needed to best preserve this heritage and its futur
 e particularly in regard to the health and safety of our Fishermen\, our s
 cientific observers\, our fishing industry as well as our fish. Stage Scre
 en Project of the film and Short Q&A with those involved. Musicians (in or
  related to the film and fishing songs) Mary Harp Player Compass Bros Mich
 ael O’Leary with Gary Dolinsky Brian King and Nathon Cohen of Mr. FoxPet
 er and Audi Sousa Sponsor/Partner Organizations and Businesses B-Roll Film
 s Manship Artists Residency Neptunes Harvest Extreme Gloucester Fishing/Sa
 lt Maritime Gloucester Schooner Adventure\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEve
 nt page: https://northofboston.org/event/gloucester-film-release-of-the-ne
 tworks-art-fishing-community/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/gloucester-film-release-of-the-network
 s-art-fishing-community/
END:VEVENT
