DTSTART:20261206T000000
DTEND:20261206T000000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:5464573756b995d5988321d6e211a3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to whisk\, roll\, and decorate your way into classic
  festive cheer! Join us for a cozy\, hands-on Yule Log class in Highfield
 ’s kitchen. You’ll learn the art of crafting this classic holiday dess
 ert from scratch — sponge cake\, rich filling\, and all the trimmings. J
 oin Highfield’s Culinary Director and professional pastry chef for step-
 by-step guidance\, tips on flavor variations\, baking and decorating techn
 iques\, and presentation. Take home your very own mini Yule Log – perfec
 t for gifting or indulging! No experience needed\; just bring your holiday
  spirit. Register online today or call 508-495-1878 ext. 2.\n\nSources: Ca
 pe Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/yule-log-
 workshop-with-kate-rickard/52757/
LOCATION:Highfield Hall & Gardens\, 56 Highfield Drive\, Falmouth\, MA\, 0
 2540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/yule-log-workshop-with-kate-ricka
 rd/52757/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deck the Halls at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261207T090000
DTEND:20261207T153000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:0341350cb87dbf563ca9d35ac1ef36@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Holiday Season as we proudly present our 
 8th annual holiday celebration\, Deck the Halls\, a Museum-wide holiday in
 stallation! Travel back in time to a castle filled with candlelight and lu
 sh\, opulent textures inspired by the great medieval and Renaissance castl
 es of Europe. We are delighted to partner again with Elaine Quinn Interior
 s\, a boutique residential interior design firm based in Manchester-by-the
 -Sea\, to bring heightened inspiration and artistry to this year’s museu
 m-wide holiday installation. Abundant greenery and sumptuous layers of dé
 cor create a richly immersive seasonal experience throughout the Museum. W
 ander through rooms adorned with white birch and Christmas trees\, sparkli
 ng fairy lights\, hydrangea-lace garlands\, and elegant bows\, with each s
 pace transformed by its own unique holiday theme. This celebration also em
 braces the traditions of Hanukkah\, with two beautifully displayed menorah
 s adding their own warm glow to the Museum’s festive splendor. From natu
 re’s bounty of fruits and greenery to the warm glow of candlelight\, eve
 ry detail creates a feast for the senses. Along the way\, encounter a roya
 l guard of nutcrackers\, a gingerbread house replica of the Museum\, and p
 layful elves and gnomes up to mischief\, adding a touch of whimsy for litt
 le ones. In addition to the holiday installation\, guests can enjoy the te
 mporary exhibition\, “Brave-Too-Much”: The Legend of John Coffee Hays.
  Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to fully experience the h
 oliday installation and exhibition Extended Tuesday and Thursday Tour Hour
 s: New this year\, visitors can enjoy extended hours on Tuesdays and Thurs
 days\, with last entry at 7:15 p.m. These extended guided and self-guided 
 tour hours offer greater opportunities to experience the Museum after dark
 \, when holiday décor glows with flickering candlelight and twinkling lig
 hts. Upon arrival\, visitors will discover the path and outdoor Courtyard
 \, arches and towers aglow with festive holiday lighting\, creating a trul
 y magical seasonal atmosphere. Visitors will have more time to explore the
  Museum’s holiday decorations and experience the beauty of this historic
  site after dark. Admission pricing varies\, please visit our website for 
 accurate pricing. Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to take 
 in the full holiday grandeur. Museum member benefits apply.\n\nSources: No
 rth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-
 at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-12-07/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-at-hammond-castle-museu
 m/2026-12-07/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music with Morgan
DTSTART:20261207T093000
DTEND:20261207T101500
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:85ac7425811123afac780079096011@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Morgan for a musical story time your kids will be talking
  about all week – singing\, dancing\, finger plays\, and short\, engagin
 g stories that target specific learning targets and early literacy skills.
  Morgan’s background in both music and special education work together t
 o make a high-quality\, engaging and educational class for your little one
 . We can’t wait to see you! Morgan’s Bio: Morgan Lynch\, MEd is a loca
 l early childhood music teacher that loves to foster community\, connectio
 n\, and playfulness in music classes. Through the use of shared instrument
 s\, fingerplays and books\, Morgan will guide families toward early childh
 ood milestones and development through music.\n\nSources: North of Boston
 \nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/music-with-morgan/2026-12-07
 /
LOCATION:Firehouse Center for the Arts\, 1 Market Square\, Newburyport\, M
 A\, 01950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/music-with-morgan/2026-12-07/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vienna Boys Choir
DTSTART:20261207T193000
DTEND:20261207T213000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:2b8acbf13d36051bd7b86dafb52b15@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The angelic-voiced musicians of the Vienna Boys Choir celebrat
 e the magic of the holiday season with a delightful program of Austrian fo
 lk songs\, classical masterpieces\, Christmas hymns\, and holiday carols. 
 For six centuries\, these young cultural ambassadors have been adored the 
 world over for their wide range of repertoire\, purity of tone\, and gener
 osity of musical spirit. The Vienna Boys Choir is one of the most celebrat
 ed and historic choirs in the world. Boys have sung at Vienna’s Imperial
  Chapel since at least 1296\, and in 1498 Holy Roman Emperor Maximilian I 
 formally established a Court Chapel in Vienna\, specifying that boys be in
 cluded among its singers. This act laid the foundation for the Vienna Boys
  Choir\, whose early members traveled with the imperial court to perform a
 t coronations\, weddings\, state ceremonies\, and other important occasion
 s throughout the Holy Roman Empire. Over the centuries\, the Viennese cour
 t attracted many of Europe’s greatest musical figures\, including Heinri
 ch Isaac\, Johann Joseph Fux\, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\, and Anton Bruckne
 r. Joseph Haydn\, Michael Haydn\, and Franz Schubert all sang as boys with
  the choir\, linking the ensemble directly to some of the most important n
 ames in classical music history. Today\, the Vienna Boys Choir is a privat
 e\, nonprofit organization and an entire educational campus devoted to cho
 ral training. Its schools serve 330 boys and girls ages six to nineteen\, 
 all of whom receive individual voice lessons and sing in one of the campus
  choirs. In addition to the four internationally touring boys’ choirs\, 
 the institution includes the Vienna Girls Choir\, Chorus Primus\, and Chor
 us Juventus. Its educational tradition is recognized by UNESCO as cultural
  heritage and is open to students regardless of origin\, gender\, national
 ity\, or religion. The 90 active boy choristers are divided among four tou
 ring choirs\, each performing under the name Vienna Boys Choir. Together\,
  they give nearly 300 concerts each year for audiences around the world. S
 ince 1924\, the choirs have completed more than 1\,000 tours in 100 countr
 ies and performed more than 29\,000 concerts. In Vienna\, the choirs conti
 nue their historic role by singing Sunday Mass in the Imperial Chapel with
  members of the Vienna Philharmonic and the Vienna State Opera men’s cho
 rus. They also appear regularly in major symphonic concerts\, at the Salzb
 urg Festival\, and with the Vienna Philharmonic’s New Year’s Concert. 
 In 2023\, the Choir celebrated its 525th anniversary\, marked by major rec
 ording and publishing projects. In 2024\, the Vienna Boys Choir and Vienna
  Girls Choir jointly received the European Culture Award. Erasmus Baumgart
 ner was appointed Artistic Director in 2023.\n\nSources: North of Boston\n
 Event page: https://northofboston.org/event/vienna-boys-choir/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/vienna-boys-choir/
END:VEVENT
