BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261210T111500
DTEND:20261210T161500
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:af864a24ba6326dd65065a720c30c1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-12-10/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 2-10/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Captain Elias Davis House Tour
DTSTART:20261211T140000
DTEND:20261211T143000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:db16d16a89c4e253908b5fd6e9e1da@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:What can a house tell us about the people who lived there? Ste
 p inside the Capt. Elias Davis House and discover how architecture\, craft
 smanship\, and everyday objects reveal the lives of one Gloucester family 
 and the changing history of Cape Ann. This docent-led experience invites v
 isitors to look closely at the details that transform a historic building 
 into a story of community\, commerce\, and home.\n\nSources: North of Bost
 on\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/captain-elias-davis-house-
 tour/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/captain-elias-davis-house-tour/2026-12
 -11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deck the Halls at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261211T090000
DTEND:20261211T153000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:aef0c3fa2cd4069f3902f0e657368b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Holiday Season as we proudly present our 
 8th annual holiday celebration\, Deck the Halls\, a Museum-wide holiday in
 stallation! Travel back in time to a castle filled with candlelight and lu
 sh\, opulent textures inspired by the great medieval and Renaissance castl
 es of Europe. We are delighted to partner again with Elaine Quinn Interior
 s\, a boutique residential interior design firm based in Manchester-by-the
 -Sea\, to bring heightened inspiration and artistry to this year’s museu
 m-wide holiday installation. Abundant greenery and sumptuous layers of dé
 cor create a richly immersive seasonal experience throughout the Museum. W
 ander through rooms adorned with white birch and Christmas trees\, sparkli
 ng fairy lights\, hydrangea-lace garlands\, and elegant bows\, with each s
 pace transformed by its own unique holiday theme. This celebration also em
 braces the traditions of Hanukkah\, with two beautifully displayed menorah
 s adding their own warm glow to the Museum’s festive splendor. From natu
 re’s bounty of fruits and greenery to the warm glow of candlelight\, eve
 ry detail creates a feast for the senses. Along the way\, encounter a roya
 l guard of nutcrackers\, a gingerbread house replica of the Museum\, and p
 layful elves and gnomes up to mischief\, adding a touch of whimsy for litt
 le ones. In addition to the holiday installation\, guests can enjoy the te
 mporary exhibition\, “Brave-Too-Much”: The Legend of John Coffee Hays.
  Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to fully experience the h
 oliday installation and exhibition Extended Tuesday and Thursday Tour Hour
 s: New this year\, visitors can enjoy extended hours on Tuesdays and Thurs
 days\, with last entry at 7:15 p.m. These extended guided and self-guided 
 tour hours offer greater opportunities to experience the Museum after dark
 \, when holiday décor glows with flickering candlelight and twinkling lig
 hts. Upon arrival\, visitors will discover the path and outdoor Courtyard
 \, arches and towers aglow with festive holiday lighting\, creating a trul
 y magical seasonal atmosphere. Visitors will have more time to explore the
  Museum’s holiday decorations and experience the beauty of this historic
  site after dark. Admission pricing varies\, please visit our website for 
 accurate pricing. Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to take 
 in the full holiday grandeur. Museum member benefits apply.\n\nSources: No
 rth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-
 at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-at-hammond-castle-museu
 m/2026-12-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Cafferty and The Beaver Brown Band
DTSTART:20261211T200000
DTEND:20261211T220000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:94c1d975ad19e50ff590600ba94f71@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:18+\, Positive I.D. Required The legendary Rhode Island multi-
 platinum rock’n’roll group John Cafferty & The Beaver Brown Band began
  their career in 1973 and achieved mainstream success in the 1980s with th
 e “Eddie & The Cruisers – Motion Picture Soundtrack”. The hit single
  “ON THE DARK SIDE” held the “#1” position on the Billboard Rock c
 harts and the MTV video charts for five consecutive weeks. The album sold 
 over 3 million copies and was certified triple Platinum by the RIAA. The t
 itle track from the group’s 1985 follow-up album “TOUGH ALL OVER” be
 came their second “#1” single on the Billboard Rock charts and the son
 g “C-I-T-Y” reached the Billboard Top 20. John Cafferty’s solo track
  “HEARTS ON FIRE” was featured in Sylvester Stallone’s film “ROCKY
  IV” and he received his second double Platinum soundtrack award. Over t
 he years John has placed 35 songs in major motion pictures. Today John Caf
 ferty & The Beaver Brown Band continue to tour and bring their exciting li
 ve shows to fans around the world. In 2012 they were inducted into the Rho
 de Island Music Hall Of Fame. 2022 marked the release of John Cafferty & t
 he Beaver Brown Band’s GREATEST HITS on Iconoclassic Records. A comprehe
 nsive collection of all “original recordings” from their hit albums an
 d movie soundtracks. In celebration of their 50 years together John Caffer
 ty & the Beaver Brown Band will be releasing a long awaited album of brand
  new songs in the spring of 2024. The pre-released single “DAY IN THE SU
 N” has received 5 star reviews and is climbing the national classic rock
  radio and streaming charts. It is featured in the new 2024 Peter Farrelly
  film “Ricky Stanicky” starring Zac Efron and John Cena.\n\nSources: N
 orth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/john-cafferty-
 and-the-beaver-brown-band/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/john-cafferty-and-the-beaver-brown-ban
 d/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261211T110000
DTEND:20261211T170000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:4b35103ca0c0ca4690abb98d82df73@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-12-11/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-12-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Choral Society’s Winter Concert Program “When Jazz
  Meets Choir”
DTSTART:20261211T193000
DTEND:20261211T213000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:b6fa2aedff1c5a4405f4bca58dddfa@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The winter concert celebrates the fusion of traditional choral
  writing\, rich jazz harmonies\, and improvisation. Composer Will Todd’s
  Mass in Blue will be performed with a jazz band featuring piano\, bass\, 
 saxophone\, and drums\, and with internationally renowned operatic jazz so
 prano soloist Katherine Whyte. The program will also include the seasonal 
 traditions for which NCS is known: the Youth Choir of Immaculate Conceptio
 n Church\, NCS’s own small chamber ensemble\, a hushed song by candlelig
 ht\, and audience sing-alongs of familiar carols. Duke Ellington’s arran
 gement of Caravan and a jazz arrangement of O Christmas Tree \, and memora
 ble selections such as Harold Arlen’s Over the Rainbow and Leonard Berns
 tein’s Make Our Garden Grow complete the program. TWO DATES: Dec 11\, 20
 26\, 7:30 PM – 9:30 PM Immaculate Conception Church\, 42 Green St\, Newb
 uryport\, MA 01950\, USA Dec 13\, 2026\, 3:00 PM – 5:00 PM Immaculate Co
 nception Church\, 42 Green St\, Newburyport\, MA 01950\, USA\n\nSources: N
 orth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-ch
 oral-societys-winter-concert-program-when-jazz-meets-choir/2026-12-11/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-choral-societys-winter-con
 cert-program-when-jazz-meets-choir/2026-12-11/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thurston Howell
DTSTART:20261211T200000
DTEND:20261211T220000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:ac02ba833d5c144f6bfa78556bef5b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Grab your Piña Colada and set sail on a nostalgic odyssey thr
 ough the smoothest soft rock hits of the ’70s and ’80s—a time when t
 ube socks had stripes\, bikes had banana seats\, and kitchen phones had 20
 -foot curly cords. Get ready for Thurston Howell—Your Premier Yacht Rock
  Spectacular! ​Sing along to chart-topping favorites like “Silly Love 
 Songs” by Paul McCartney & Wings\, “You’re So Vain” by Carly Simon
 \, “What a Fool Believes” by The Doobie Brothers\, “I Can’t Go for
  That” by Hall & Oates\, “Brandy” by Looking Glass\, and “Baby Com
 e Back” by Player—plus unforgettable hits like “Baker Street” by G
 erry Rafferty\, “Ride Like the Wind” by Christopher Cross\, and many m
 ore smooth classics! ​Together\, they have been bringing the smooth soun
 ds of yacht rock to ports along the East Coast—from the rocky\, lobster-
 scented docks of Bar Harbor\, Maine\, all the way down to the sun-soaked\,
  palm-lined marinas of Fort Lauderdale\, Florida. Every harbor. Every suns
 et cruise. Every deck party in between. They were there. They were cool. T
 hey showed up with 100% pure uncut yacht rock…because you can’t fake s
 mooth! Bring your sailor hats and captain’s hats\, gather your crew\, an
 d set sail with Thurston Howell for a Yacht Rock Spectacular. All hands on
  deck! Thelarcom.org/thurstonhowell\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent pag
 e: https://northofboston.org/event/thurston-howell/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/thurston-howell/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tony DeSare: Holiday Pops
DTSTART:20261211T193000
DTEND:20261211T213000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:b708901277f087cab0b74da3b8a1bf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Tony DeSare delivers a fresh take on the Great American Songbo
 ok\, blending jazz\, swing\, and pop with charm and virtuosity. From Sinat
 ra to Billy Joel\, plus his own award-winning songs\, DeSare’s program c
 elebrates timeless melodies and heartfelt storytelling. A dynamic evening 
 of all your holiday favorites with one of today’s most engaging performe
 rs. ABOUT THE ARTIST Tony DeSare performs with infectious joy\, wry playfu
 lness and robust musicality. Named “Rising Star Male Vocalist” in Down
 beat magazine\, DeSare has lived up to this distinction by winning critica
 l and popular acclaim for his concert performances throughout North Americ
 a and abroad. From jazz clubs to Carnegie Hall to Las Vegas and headlining
  major symphony orchestras\, DeSare has brought his fresh take on old scho
 ol class around the globe. DeSare has four top ten Billboard jazz albums u
 nder his belt and has been featured on the CBS Early Show\, NPR\, A Prairi
 e Home Companion\, and the Today Show\, and his music has been posted by s
 ocial media celebrity juggernaut George Takei. DeSare has also collaborate
 d with YouTube supergroup Postmodern Jukebox. He has been a featured guest
  artist with over 100 symphony orchestras with some highlights including t
 he Cleveland Orchestra\, The New York Pops\, The San Francisco Symphony\, 
 The Houston Symphony\, and the Chicago Symphony. Notwithstanding his criti
 cally acclaimed turns as a singer/pianist\, DeSare is also an award-winnin
 g composer. He not only won first place in the USA Songwriting Contest\, b
 ut has written the theme song for the motion picture My Date With Drew and
  several broadcast commercials\, and has scored five films. His sound is r
 omantic\, swinging\, and sensual\, but what sets DeSare apart is his abili
 ty to write original material that sounds fresh and contemporary\, yet pay
 s homage to the Great American Songbook. Tony has a strong presence on soc
 ial media and continues to release his “song diaries\,” recordings fro
 m his home studio that started in 2020 and now number in the 100s. Tony ha
 s numerous recordings available on all platforms and playlists. Tony DeSar
 e is a Yamaha Artist.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nor
 thofboston.org/event/tony-desare-holiday-pops-2/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/tony-desare-holiday-pops-2/
END:VEVENT
