BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samson et Dalila
DTSTART:20261219T110000
DTEND:20261219T130000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:608b0e5e68cb8438aaf381f156a451@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Music by Camille Saint-Saëns | Libretto by Ferdinand Lemaire 
 Saint-Saëns’s spectacular take on the biblical hero of legendary streng
 th and the seductive Philistine whose beauty overpowers him returns in the
  Met’s larger-than-life production. Featuring a massive orchestra and ch
 orus and some of opera’s most spellbinding tunes\, this masterpiece is a
  feast for the eyes and ears. Giacomo Sagripanti conducts an electrifying 
 cast led by the formidable star pairing of mezzosoprano Aigul Akhmetshina 
 and tenor Clay Hilley\, transmitted live to cinemas worldwide. Conductor: 
 Giacomo Sagripanti Production: Darko Tresnjak Dalila: Aigul Akhmetshina Se
 t Designer: Alexander Dodge Samson: Clay Hilley Costume Designer: Linda Ch
 o High Priest of Dagon: Quinn Kelsey Lighting Designer: Donald Holder Abim
 élech: Alfred Walker Choreographer Austin McCormick Old Hebrew: Morris Ro
 binson C. Graham Berwind\, III Chorus Director: Tilman Michael\n\nSources:
  North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/samson-et-da
 lila/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/samson-et-dalila/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seasonal Saturday Tours!
DTSTART:20261219T110000
DTEND:20261219T160000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:9a7afffdf088966c1016fa37618bd0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Fall and Winter Guided Tours at the Museum of Old Newbury Begi
 nning in mid-October\, 2026\, the Museum of Old Newbury will open its door
 s for guided tours every Saturday. Tours begin on the hour from 11:00 a.m.
  to 4:00 p.m. (last tour departs at 3:00 p.m.). Please note: certain dates
  are excluded\, and tours are weather permitting. Step back in time as you
 r knowledgeable guide leads you through two floors of our 1808 brick Feder
 al-style home\, where every room is filled with objects\, stories\, and me
 mories of Old Newbury. Along the way\, you’ll hear tales of the families
  who lived here\, discover treasures from our collection\, and gain new in
 sight into the rich history of Newburyport and the surrounding area. Wheth
 er you’re a first-time visitor or a longtime resident\, this is your cha
 nce to experience the museum in a whole new way—through a carefully cura
 ted\, guided experience designed to bring history to life.\n\nSources: Nor
 th of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/seasonal-saturda
 y-tours-2/2026-12-19/
LOCATION:Museum of Old Newbury\, 98 High Street\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/seasonal-saturday-tours-2/2026-12-19/
END:VEVENT
