BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261220T110000
DTEND:20261220T170000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:6d918232a10e55eba6ff01ad634381@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-12-20/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-12-20/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:White Christmas
DTSTART:20261220T130000
DTEND:20261220T160000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:e4e8884321f8ca3c4c25d4025486bf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season with the timeless holiday classic White C
 hristmas. Starring Bing Crosby\, Danny Kaye\, Rosemary Clooney\, and Vera-
 Ellen\, this beloved musical follows two entertainers who team up with a s
 ister act to save a Vermont inn. Filled with unforgettable songs\, dazzlin
 g dance numbers\, and festive charm\, it’s a holiday tradition for all a
 ges.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/white-christmas/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/white-christmas/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261220T111500
DTEND:20261220T161500
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:4856d531827c30b3ac2d27bbe1321a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-12-20/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 2-20/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deck the Halls at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261221T090000
DTEND:20261221T153000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:839b6eb65a54ad819bdbabd2712deb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Holiday Season as we proudly present our 
 8th annual holiday celebration\, Deck the Halls\, a Museum-wide holiday in
 stallation! Travel back in time to a castle filled with candlelight and lu
 sh\, opulent textures inspired by the great medieval and Renaissance castl
 es of Europe. We are delighted to partner again with Elaine Quinn Interior
 s\, a boutique residential interior design firm based in Manchester-by-the
 -Sea\, to bring heightened inspiration and artistry to this year’s museu
 m-wide holiday installation. Abundant greenery and sumptuous layers of dé
 cor create a richly immersive seasonal experience throughout the Museum. W
 ander through rooms adorned with white birch and Christmas trees\, sparkli
 ng fairy lights\, hydrangea-lace garlands\, and elegant bows\, with each s
 pace transformed by its own unique holiday theme. This celebration also em
 braces the traditions of Hanukkah\, with two beautifully displayed menorah
 s adding their own warm glow to the Museum’s festive splendor. From natu
 re’s bounty of fruits and greenery to the warm glow of candlelight\, eve
 ry detail creates a feast for the senses. Along the way\, encounter a roya
 l guard of nutcrackers\, a gingerbread house replica of the Museum\, and p
 layful elves and gnomes up to mischief\, adding a touch of whimsy for litt
 le ones. In addition to the holiday installation\, guests can enjoy the te
 mporary exhibition\, “Brave-Too-Much”: The Legend of John Coffee Hays.
  Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to fully experience the h
 oliday installation and exhibition Extended Tuesday and Thursday Tour Hour
 s: New this year\, visitors can enjoy extended hours on Tuesdays and Thurs
 days\, with last entry at 7:15 p.m. These extended guided and self-guided 
 tour hours offer greater opportunities to experience the Museum after dark
 \, when holiday décor glows with flickering candlelight and twinkling lig
 hts. Upon arrival\, visitors will discover the path and outdoor Courtyard
 \, arches and towers aglow with festive holiday lighting\, creating a trul
 y magical seasonal atmosphere. Visitors will have more time to explore the
  Museum’s holiday decorations and experience the beauty of this historic
  site after dark. Admission pricing varies\, please visit our website for 
 accurate pricing. Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to take 
 in the full holiday grandeur. Museum member benefits apply.\n\nSources: No
 rth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-
 at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-12-21/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-at-hammond-castle-museu
 m/2026-12-21/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music with Morgan
DTSTART:20261221T093000
DTEND:20261221T101500
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:42896c89433cb8d7ed6add351c6e5d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Morgan for a musical story time your kids will be talking
  about all week – singing\, dancing\, finger plays\, and short\, engagin
 g stories that target specific learning targets and early literacy skills.
  Morgan’s background in both music and special education work together t
 o make a high-quality\, engaging and educational class for your little one
 . We can’t wait to see you! Morgan’s Bio: Morgan Lynch\, MEd is a loca
 l early childhood music teacher that loves to foster community\, connectio
 n\, and playfulness in music classes. Through the use of shared instrument
 s\, fingerplays and books\, Morgan will guide families toward early childh
 ood milestones and development through music.\n\nSources: North of Boston
 \nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/music-with-morgan/2026-12-21
 /
LOCATION:Firehouse Center for the Arts\, 1 Market Square\, Newburyport\, M
 A\, 01950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/music-with-morgan/2026-12-21/
END:VEVENT
