BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seasonal Saturday Tours!
DTSTART:20270116T110000
DTEND:20270116T160000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:a0e1c612f1e4d8809f095e7123d5b3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Fall and Winter Guided Tours at the Museum of Old Newbury Begi
 nning in mid-October\, 2026\, the Museum of Old Newbury will open its door
 s for guided tours every Saturday. Tours begin on the hour from 11:00 a.m.
  to 4:00 p.m. (last tour departs at 3:00 p.m.). Please note: certain dates
  are excluded\, and tours are weather permitting. Step back in time as you
 r knowledgeable guide leads you through two floors of our 1808 brick Feder
 al-style home\, where every room is filled with objects\, stories\, and me
 mories of Old Newbury. Along the way\, you’ll hear tales of the families
  who lived here\, discover treasures from our collection\, and gain new in
 sight into the rich history of Newburyport and the surrounding area. Wheth
 er you’re a first-time visitor or a longtime resident\, this is your cha
 nce to experience the museum in a whole new way—through a carefully cura
 ted\, guided experience designed to bring history to life.\n\nSources: Nor
 th of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/seasonal-saturda
 y-tours-2/2027-01-16/
LOCATION:Museum of Old Newbury\, 98 High Street\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/seasonal-saturday-tours-2/2027-01-16/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Beautiful Losers — A Tribute to Bob Seger & The Silver Bulle
 t Band
DTSTART:20270116T200000
DTEND:20270116T200000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:c5b379768b0cefe45de1c00a7a620b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:With an all-star cast of players\, The Beautiful Losers have t
 aken America by storm with their incredible tribute to the music of Bob Se
 ger & The Silver Bullet Band. You will hear ALL the hits plus live showsto
 ppers that Bob and his band made famous during this amazing night of music
  with The Beautiful Losers. Devin Cordeiro – Lead Vocals (Last Laugh) Da
 vid Stefanelli – Drums (Robert Ellis Orrall\, RTZ w/ Brad Delp & Barry G
 oudreau formerly of the band BOSTON\, Peter Wolf’s Houseparty 5 of J. Ge
 ils Band\, Sully Erna of Godsmack) David Ayotte – Sax\, Vocals (The Cont
 inentals) Carl Ayotte – Sax\, Guitar\, Vocals (All Summer Long\, Captain
  Morgan & The Rum Runners) Steve Baker – Keyboards (BeatleJuice w/ Brad 
 Delp of BOSTON\, Fortune\, Ben Orr of The Cars) Nate Comp – Guitar\, Voc
 als (Craving Lucy\, Rotten Apple) Kevin Elder – Bass (Last Laugh\, Groov
 e Alliance) Bill Plourde – Guitar\, Vocals (Fortune\, Tangerine)\n\nSour
 ces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/the-beau
 tiful-losers-a-tribute-to-bob-seger-the-silver-bullet-band/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/the-beautiful-losers-a-tribute-to-bob-
 seger-the-silver-bullet-band/
END:VEVENT
