BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jambalaya Horns Mardi Gras Party
DTSTART:20270206T200000
DTEND:20270206T220000
DTSTAMP:20261110T190930Z
UID:5997d8d196dad55e1fe76ad49c441e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:New Orleans-flavored Funk\, Soul\, and Brassy 2nd-Lines by the
  Jambalaya Horns will have you feeling like you’re in New Orleans this M
 ardi Gras season! Formed in 2013 and fronted by Carlos Menezes Jr. on lead
  vocals and horns\, the group strives to capture the essence and soul of t
 he diverse musical culture of the Crescent City. The core group features M
 artina Gallo (keys)\, Rick Geraghty (drums)\, Gary Wolsieffer (bass/tuba)
 \, Derek Hayden (drums/percussion)\, Matt Naeger (trumpet)\, Henley Dougla
 s Jr. (saxes)\, Anthony Prestigiovanni (trumpet)\, and Nick Capello (tenor
  sax). This show will also feature surprise guest soloists and vocalists! 
 You’ll feel like you’re in New Orleans this Mardi Gras Season! Carlos 
 Menezes Jr’s BrassFed Nation is a horn-driven groove machine with a uniq
 ue sound incorporating the styles and traditions of early Jazz\, New Orlea
 ns Funk & Soul\, Rhythm & Blues\, Calypso\, and Jamaican Ska! Founded in 2
 013\, The BrassFed Nation is dedicated to the advancement of horn-driven m
 usic through exposure and outreach in both education and local musical cul
 ture! The collective features 3 unique ensembles\; Cape Ann Big Band\, The
  Jambalaya Horns\, and The 15-Piece DubTone Orchestra – all striving to 
 inspire and connect musicians of all ages through performances\, private s
 tudio lessons\, workshops\, and interactive clinics.\n\nSources: North of 
 Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/jambalaya-horns-mardi-
 gras-party/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/jambalaya-horns-mardi-gras-party/
END:VEVENT
